Caelza: the Connect page (vision §3.4, the Guide everywhere): your apps
through Maton, your smart home through Home Assistant and a 3D printer on
your Wi-Fi, each from one box or two on the dashboard, with no shell.

The page (web/src/pages/connect/, an overlay) writes what the connect scripts
write through the config API the dashboard already has: the `[[mcp.servers]]`
row by name (`POST /api/config/map-key`, since it is a keyed list no property
path can create), then one atomic `PATCH /api/config` for its url, transport,
timeout and encrypted Authorization header, its bundle and the agent's grant;
a printer allows its one address and keeps the OctoPrint key as a secret. What
the config API cannot do is put a skill on disk, so the gateway's
api_connect.rs (an overlay module; its SKILL.md copy is placed beside it by
runtime/build.sh) answers /api/connect/skills. These hunks register the module
and its routes, route the page, put Connect in the sidebar's Configure group
and the title maps, add the API client functions, add the strings (English;
the other locales fall back) and list the logic test beside the others.
Applied after 0014 and the overlay copy.

